      "content": "Traditionalist theologians often characterize the secular approach to marriage as a \"relativistic\" or \"nihilistic\" worldview that has abandoned objective moral truths for subjective personal preference. They argue that by reducing marriage to a matter of individual autonomy or social utility, the secular side actively destroys the objective good of human flourishing and the divine plan for procreation. This fundamental shift, they claim, replaces the binding nature of covenant with the fleeting nature of contract, leading to a moral vacuum where love becomes optional and family becomes a disposable arrangement.",
